args.content:
# Ant Design Quick Start Tutorial

## Table of Contents
1. [Introduction](#introduction)
2. [Installation](#installation)
3. [Basic Setup](#basic-setup)
4. [Essential Components](#essential-components)
5. [Layout Components](#layout-components)
6. [Form Components](#form-components)
7. [Data Display Components](#data-display-components)
8. [Feedback Components](#feedback-components)
9. [Best Practices](#best-practices)
10. [Resources](#resources)

---

## Introduction

Ant Design is a React UI library that provides high-quality components and demos for building rich, interactive user interfaces. It follows the Ant Design specification and is widely used in enterprise-level applications.

### Key Features
- 🎨 Enterprise-class UI designed for web applications
- 📱 Responsive design that works on all devices
- 🌍 Internationalization support
- 🎯 Complete set of high-quality React components
- 📖 Comprehensive documentation and design resources

---

## Installation

### Using npm
```bash
npm install antd
```

### Using yarn
```bash
yarn add antd
```

### Using pnpm
```bash
pnpm add antd
```

---

## Basic Setup

### 1. Import CSS
In your main entry file (e.g., `src/index.js` or `src/main.tsx`):

```jsx
import 'antd/dist/reset.css'; // Ant Design v5+
// or for older versions:
// import 'antd/dist/antd.css';
```

### 2. Basic Component Usage
```jsx
import React from 'react';
import { Button, Space, DatePicker } from 'antd';

function App() {
  return (
    <div style={{ padding: 24 }}>
      <Space direction="vertical" size="middle">
        <h1>Welcome to Ant Design!</h1>
        <Button type="primary">Primary Button</Button>
        <DatePicker />
      </Space>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

---

## Essential Components

### Button
Buttons are used for triggering actions.

```jsx
import { Button, Space } from 'antd';

function ButtonExample() {
  return (
    <Space>
      <Button type="primary">Primary Button</Button>
      <Button>Default Button</Button>
      <Button type="dashed">Dashed Button</Button>
      <Button type="text">Text Button</Button>
      <Button type="link">Link Button</Button>
    </Space>
  );
}
```

### Icon
Icons provide semantic vector graphics.

```jsx
import { Space, Button } from 'antd';
import { HomeOutlined, SettingOutlined, UserOutlined } from '@ant-design/icons';

function IconExample() {
  return (
    <Space>
      <Button icon={<HomeOutlined />}>Home</Button>
      <Button icon={<SettingOutlined />}>Settings</Button>
      <Button icon={<UserOutlined />}>Profile</Button>
    </Space>
  );
}
```

### Space
Space provides a lightweight way to handle component spacing.

```jsx
import { Space, Card, Button } from 'antd';

function SpaceExample() {
  return (
    <Space direction="vertical" size="large" style={{ display: 'flex' }}>
      <Card title="Vertical Space">
        <Space direction="vertical">
          <Button>Button 1</Button>
          <Button>Button 2</Button>
          <Button>Button 3</Button>
        </Space>
      </Card>

      <Card title="Horizontal Space">
        <Space>
          <Button>Button 1</Button>
          <Button>Button 2</Button>
          <Button>Button 3</Button>
        </Space>
      </Card>
    </Space>
  );
}
```

---

## Layout Components

### Layout
Layout components help you organize your page structure.

```jsx
import { Layout, Menu } from 'antd';
import { HomeOutlined, InfoCircleOutlined } from '@ant-design/icons';

const { Header, Footer, Sider, Content } = Layout;

function LayoutExample() {
  return (
    <Layout style={{ minHeight: '100vh' }}>
      <Sider width={200}>
        <Menu
          mode="inline"
          defaultSelectedKeys={['1']}
          items={[
            {
              key: '1',
              icon: <HomeOutlined />,
              label: 'Home',
            },
            {
              key: '2',
              icon: <InfoCircleOutlined />,
              label: 'About',
            },
          ]}
        />
      </Sider>
      <Layout>
        <Header style={{ background: '#fff', padding: 0 }} />
        <Content style={{ margin: '24px 16px 0' }}>
          <div style={{ padding: 24, background: '#fff', minHeight: 360 }}>
            Content Area
          </div>
        </Content>
        <Footer style={{ textAlign: 'center' }}>
          Ant Design ©2023 Created by Your Name
        </Footer>
      </Layout>
    </Layout>
  );
}
```

### Grid
Ant Design provides a 24-column grid system.

```jsx
import { Row, Col, Card } from 'antd';

function GridExample() {
  return (
    <Row gutter={[16, 16]}>
      <Col span={8}>
        <Card title="Card 1">Content 1</Card>
      </Col>
      <Col span={8}>
        <Card title="Card 2">Content 2</Card>
      </Col>
      <Col span={8}>
        <Card title="Card 3">Content 3</Card>
      </Col>
      <Col span={12}>
        <Card title="Card 4">Content 4 (12 columns)</Card>
      </Col>
      <Col span={12}>
        <Card title="Card 5">Content 5 (12 columns)</Card>
      </Col>
    </Row>
  );
}
```

---

## Form Components

### Form
Ant Design provides powerful form components with validation.

```jsx
import { Form, Input, Button, Select, DatePicker } from 'antd';

const { Option } = Select;

function FormExample() {
  const onFinish = (values) => {
    console.log('Form values:', values);
  };

  return (
    <Form
      name="basic"
      labelCol={{ span: 8 }}
      wrapperCol={{ span: 16 }}
      onFinish={onFinish}
      autoComplete="off"
    >
      <Form.Item
        label="Username"
        name="username"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please input your username!' }]}
      >
        <Input />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Email"
        name="email"
        rules={[
          { required: true, message: 'Please input your email!' },
          { type: 'email', message: 'Please enter a valid email!' }
        ]}
      >
        <Input />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Gender"
        name="gender"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please select gender!' }]}
      >
        <Select placeholder="Select your gender">
          <Option value="male">Male</Option>
          <Option value="female">Female</Option>
          <Option value="other">Other</Option>
        </Select>
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Birthday"
        name="birthday"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please select your birthday!' }]}
      >
        <DatePicker />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item wrapperCol={{ offset: 8, span: 16 }}>
        <Button type="primary" htmlType="submit">
          Submit
        </Button>
      </Form.Item>
    </Form>
  );
}
```

### Input
Input components for data entry.

```jsx
import { Input, Space } from 'antd';
import { UserOutlined, LockOutlined, MailOutlined } from '@ant-design/icons';

function InputExample() {
  return (
    <Space direction="vertical" style={{ width: '100%' }}>
      <Input placeholder="Basic input" />
      <Input
        placeholder="Input with icon"
        prefix={<UserOutlined />}
      />
      <Input.Password
        placeholder="Password input"
        prefix={<LockOutlined />}
      />
      <Input
        placeholder="Email input"
        prefix={<MailOutlined />}
        suffix="@example.com"
      />
      <Input.Search placeholder="Search input" />
    </Space>
  );
}
```

---

## Data Display Components

### Table
Table components for displaying structured data.

```jsx
import { Table, Tag, Space } from 'antd';

function TableExample() {
  const columns = [
    {
      title: 'Name',
      dataIndex: 'name',
      key: 'name',
    },
    {
      title: 'Age',
      dataIndex: 'age',
      key: 'age',
    },
    {
      title: 'Address',
      dataIndex: 'address',
      key: 'address',
    },
    {
      title: 'Tags',
      key: 'tags',
      dataIndex: 'tags',
      render: (_, { tags }) => (
        <>
          {tags.map((tag) => (
            <Tag color="blue" key={tag}>
              {tag}
            </Tag>
          ))}
        </>
      ),
    },
    {
      title: 'Action',
      key: 'action',
      render: (_, record) => (
        <Space size="middle">
          <a>Edit</a>
          <a>Delete</a>
        </Space>
      ),
    },
  ];

  const data = [
    {
      key: '1',
      name: 'John Brown',
      age: 32,
      address: 'New York No. 1 Lake Park',
      tags: ['developer', 'react'],
    },
    {
      key: '2',
      name: 'Jim Green',
      age: 42,
      address: 'London No. 1 Lake Park',
      tags: ['designer', 'ui'],
    },
    {
      key: '3',
      name: 'Joe Black',
      age: 32,
      address: 'Sydney No. 1 Lake Park',
      tags: ['manager', 'leader'],
    },
  ];

  return <Table columns={columns} dataSource={data} />;
}
```

### List
List components for displaying a series of content.

```jsx
import { List, Avatar, Space } from 'antd';
import { LikeOutlined, MessageOutlined, StarOutlined } from '@ant-design/icons';

const listData = [
  {
    title: 'Ant Design Title 1',
    description: 'Ant Design, a design language for background applications, is refined by Ant UED Team.',
    content: 'We supply a series of design principles, practical patterns and high quality design resources.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Ant Design Title 2',
    description: 'Ant Design, a design language for background applications, is refined by Ant UED Team.',
    content: 'We supply a series of design principles, practical patterns and high quality design resources.',
  },
];

const IconText = ({ icon, text }) => (
  <Space>
    {React.createElement(icon)}
    {text}
  </Space>
);

function ListExample() {
  return (
    <List
      itemLayout="vertical"
      size="large"
      dataSource={listData}
      renderItem={(item) => (
        <List.Item
          key={item.title}
          actions={[
            <IconText icon={StarOutlined} text="156" key="list-vertical-star-o" />,
            <IconText icon={LikeOutlined} text="156" key="list-vertical-like-o" />,
            <IconText icon={MessageOutlined} text="2" key="list-vertical-message" />,
          ]}
        >
          <List.Item.Meta
            avatar={<Avatar src="https://joeschmoe.io/api/v1/random" />}
            title={<a href={item.href}>{item.title}</a>}
            description={item.description}
          />
          {item.content}
        </List.Item>
      )}
    />
  );
}
```

---

## Feedback Components

### Message
Global feedback for operations.

```jsx
import { Button, message, Space } from 'antd';

function MessageExample() {
  const success = () => {
    message.success('This is a success message');
  };

  const error = () => {
    message.error('This is an error message');
  };

  const warning = () => {
    message.warning('This is a warning message');
  };

  return (
    <Space>
      <Button onClick={success}>Success</Button>
      <Button onClick={error}>Error</Button>
      <Button onClick={warning}>Warning</Button>
    </Space>
  );
}
```

### Modal
Modal dialogs for user interactions.

```jsx
import { Button, Modal, Space } from 'antd';
import { useState } from 'react';

function ModalExample() {
  const [isModalOpen, setIsModalOpen] = useState(false);

  const showModal = () => {
    setIsModalOpen(true);
  };

  const handleOk = () => {
    setIsModalOpen(false);
  };

  const handleCancel = () => {
    setIsModalOpen(false);
  };

  return (
    <>
      <Button type="primary" onClick={showModal}>
        Open Modal
      </Button>
      <Modal
        title="Basic Modal"
        open={isModalOpen}
        onOk={handleOk}
        onCancel={handleCancel}
      >
        <p>Some contents...</p>
        <p>Some contents...</p>
        <p>Some contents...</p>
      </Modal>
    </>
  );
}
```

### Notification
Notification components for global feedback.

```jsx
import { Button, notification, Space } from 'antd';

function NotificationExample() {
  const openNotification = () => {
    notification.open({
      message: 'Notification Title',
      description:
        'This is the content of the notification. This is the content of the notification. This is the content of the notification.',
      onClick: () => {
        console.log('Notification Clicked!');
      },
    });
  };

  return (
    <Button type="primary" onClick={openNotification}>
      Open Notification
    </Button>
  );
}
```

---

## Best Practices

### 1. Use ConfigProvider for Global Configuration
```jsx
import { ConfigProvider } from 'antd';

function App() {
  return (
    <ConfigProvider
      theme={{
        token: {
          colorPrimary: '#1677ff',
        },
      }}
    >
      {/* Your app components */}
    </ConfigProvider>
  );
}
```

### 2. Responsive Design
```jsx
import { Row, Col, Card } from 'antd';

function ResponsiveExample() {
  return (
    <Row gutter={[16, 16]}>
      <Col xs={24} sm={12} md={8} lg={6}>
        <Card>Responsive Card</Card>
      </Col>
      <Col xs={24} sm={12} md={8} lg={6}>
        <Card>Responsive Card</Card>
      </Col>
    </Row>
  );
}
```

### 3. Loading States
```jsx
import { Spin, Button } from 'antd';
import { useState } from 'react';

function LoadingExample() {
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);

  const handleClick = () => {
    setLoading(true);
    setTimeout(() => {
      setLoading(false);
    }, 2000);
  };

  return (
    <Spin spinning={loading}>
      <Button onClick={handleClick} loading={loading}>
        Click to Load
      </Button>
    </Spin>
  );
}
```

### 4. Error Boundaries
```jsx
import { Result, Button } from 'antd';

function ErrorBoundaryExample() {
  return (
    <Result
      status="error"
      title="Submission Failed"
      subTitle="Please check and modify the following information before resubmitting."
      extra={[
        <Button key="buy">Go Console</Button>,
        <Button key="again" type="primary">
          Try Again
        </Button>,
      ]}
    >
      {/* Additional error details */}
    </Result>
  );
}
```

---

## Resources

### Official Documentation
- [Ant Design Documentation](https://ant.design/)
- [Ant Design Components](https://ant.design/components/overview/)
- [Ant Design GitHub](https://github.com/ant-design/ant-design)

### Design Resources
- [Ant Design Design Principles](https://ant.design/docs/spec/introduce)
- [Ant Design Color System](https://ant.design/docs/spec/colors)
- [Ant Design Icon Library](https://ant.design/components/icon/)

### Community
- [Ant Design Discussions](https://github.com/ant-design/ant-design/discussions)
- [Stack Overflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/ant-design)
- [Ant Design Blog](https://ant.design/blog)

### Tools
- [Ant Design Pro](https://pro.ant.design/) - Enterprise-level front-end solution
- [Ant Design Mobile](https://mobile.ant.design/) - Mobile UI components
- [Ant Design Charts](https://ant.design/components/chart/) - Data visualization components

---

## Conclusion

Ant Design provides a comprehensive set of React UI components that help you build beautiful and functional web applications quickly. By following this tutorial, you should now have a solid understanding of:

- How to install and set up Ant Design
- How to use essential components
- How to create layouts and forms
- How to display data effectively
- How to provide user feedback
- Best practices for using Ant Design

Remember to always refer to the official documentation for the most up-to-date information and advanced usage patterns. Happy coding! 🚀

